## Dart Language Fundamentals

### Variables & Data Types

**Declaring Variables:**
```dart
// Type-inferred
var name = 'John';
var age = 25;
var price = 19.99;

// Explicit types
String country = 'USA';
int count = 10;
double rating = 4.5;
bool isActive = true;

// Final and const
final String city = 'NYC'; // Can't be changed after initialization
const double PI = 3.14159; // Compile-time constant

// Dynamic
dynamic value = 'Hello';
value = 123; // Can change type
```

**Null Safety:**
```dart
// Non-nullable
String name = 'John'; // Can't be null
int age = 25;

// Nullable
String? nickname; // Can be null
int? phone;

// Null assertion
String value = nickname!; // Will throw if null

// Null coalescing
String display = nickname ?? 'No nickname';

// Null-aware operators
int? length = nickname?.length; // Returns null if nickname is null
```

### Collections

**Lists:**
```dart
// Create lists
List<String> fruits = ['Apple', 'Banana', 'Orange'];
var numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
var emptyList = <int>[];

// List operations
fruits.add('Mango');
fruits.length;
fruits[0];
fruits.forEach((fruit) => print(fruit));
fruits.where((f) => f.length > 5).toList();
```

**Sets:**
```dart
Set<String> colors = {'Red', 'Green', 'Blue'};
colors.add('Yellow');
colors.contains('Red'); // true
```

**Maps:**
```dart
Map<String, int> ages = {'John': 25, 'Jane': 30};
ages['Bob'] = 35;
ages['John']; // 25
ages.keys;
ages.values;
ages.forEach((name, age) => print('$name: $age'));
```

### Functions

**Basic Functions:**
```dart
// Simple function
void greet(String name) {
  print('Hello, $name!');
}

// Return value
int add(int a, int b) {
  return a + b;
}

// Arrow function
int multiply(int a, int b) => a * b;

// Optional parameters
void printInfo(String name, [String? city]) {
  print('$name from ${city ?? 'unknown'}');
}

// Named parameters
void printDetails({required String name, int age = 0}) {
  print('$name, $age years old');
}

// Call with named parameters
printDetails(name: 'John', age: 25);

// Default parameters
void sayHello(String greeting = 'Hi') {
  print(greeting);
}
```

### Classes & OOP

**Class Definition:**
```dart
class Person {
  String name;
  int age;

  // Constructor
  Person(this.name, this.age);

  // Named constructor
  Person.guest() : name = 'Guest', age = 0;

  // Methods
  void introduce() {
    print('I am $name, $age years old');
  }

  String get info => '$name ($age)';
  
  set birthYear(int year) {
    age = DateTime.now().year - year;
  }
}

// Inheritance
class Employee extends Person {
  String role;

  Employee(String name, int age, this.role) 
    : super(name, age);

  @override
  void introduce() {
    print('I am $name, $age, working as $role');
  }
}

// Abstract class
abstract class Animal {
  void makeSound();
}

class Dog extends Animal {
  @override
  void makeSound() {
    print('Woof!');
  }
}

// Mixins
mixin Flyer {
  void fly() => print('Flying...');
}

class Bird extends Animal with Flyer {
  @override
  void makeSound() => print('Chirp!');
}
```

### Async/Await & Futures

**Futures:**
```dart
// Future represents async result
Future<String> fetchData() {
  return Future.delayed(
    Duration(seconds: 2),
    () => 'Data loaded',
  );
}

// Using then
fetchData().then((result) {
  print(result);
}).catchError((error) {
  print('Error: $error');
});

// Using async/await
void loadData() async {
  try {
    String result = await fetchData();
    print(result);
  } catch (e) {
    print('Error: $e');
  }
}
```

**Streams:**
```dart
// Stream emits multiple values over time
Stream<int> countStream() async* {
  for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    await Future.delayed(Duration(seconds: 1));
    yield i;
  }
}

// Listen to stream
countStream().listen((value) {
  print('Value: $value');
});
```

