## Navigation & Routing

### Basic Navigation

```dart
// Push to new screen
Navigator.push(
  context,
  MaterialPageRoute(builder: (context) => SecondScreen()),
);

// Pop to previous screen
Navigator.pop(context);

// Pop and return data
Navigator.pop(context, 'Return value');

// Push replacement
Navigator.pushReplacement(
  context,
  MaterialPageRoute(builder: (context) => HomeScreen()),
);
```

### Passing Data Between Screens

**Send Data:**
```dart
Navigator.push(
  context,
  MaterialPageRoute(
    builder: (context) => DetailScreen(name: 'John'),
  ),
);
```

**Receive Data:**
```dart
class DetailScreen extends StatelessWidget {
  final String name;
  
  const DetailScreen({required this.name});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Scaffold(
      body: Text('Name: $name'),
    );
  }
}
```

**Return Data:**
```dart
// From detail screen
Navigator.pop(context, 'Returned data');

// In calling screen
final result = await Navigator.push(
  context,
  MaterialPageRoute(builder: (context) => DetailScreen()),
);
print(result); // 'Returned data'
```

### Named Routes

```dart
// Define routes in main.dart
void main() {
  runApp(
    MaterialApp(
      initialRoute: '/',
      routes: {
        '/': (context) => HomeScreen(),
        '/detail': (context) => DetailScreen(),
        '/settings': (context) => SettingsScreen(),
      },
    ),
  );
}

// Navigate using named route
Navigator.pushNamed(context, '/detail');

// With arguments
Navigator.pushNamed(
  context,
  '/detail',
  arguments: {'name': 'John', 'age': 25},
);

// Receive arguments
class DetailScreen extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final args = ModalRoute.of(context)!.settings.arguments as Map;
    return Scaffold(
      body: Text('Name: ${args['name']}'),
    );
  }
}
```

### GoRouter (Modern Routing)

**Installation:** Add `go_router: ^6.0.0` to pubspec.yaml

```dart
final router = GoRouter(
  routes: [
    GoRoute(
      path: '/',
      builder: (context, state) => const HomeScreen(),
      routes: [
        GoRoute(
          path: 'detail',
          builder: (context, state) {
            final name = state.queryParameters['name'] ?? 'Guest';
            return DetailScreen(name: name);
          },
        ),
      ],
    ),
  ],
);

void main() {
  runApp(MaterialApp.router(routerConfig: router));
}

// Navigate
context.go('/');
context.go('/detail?name=John');
context.push('/detail?name=Jane');
context.pop();
```

