## Advanced Concepts & Theory

### 1. Widget Lifecycle - Complete Theory & Practice

**Lifecycle Theory:**
The widget lifecycle is the series of events that occur from widget creation to disposal. Understanding this is crucial for resource management and performance optimization.

**Complete Lifecycle Flow:**

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Application Start                     │
└────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                     │
         ┌───────────▼───────────┐
         │   buildApp()          │
         │   runApp(MyApp())     │
         └───────────┬───────────┘
                     │
         ┌───────────▼──────────────────┐
         │   MyApp creates State        │
         │   MyApp.createState()        │
         └───────────┬──────────────────┘
                     │
         ┌───────────▼──────────────────┐
         │   initState() called         │
         │   - Initialize resources     │
         │   - Setup listeners          │
         │   - Initialize controllers   │
         └───────────┬──────────────────┘
                     │
         ┌───────────▼──────────────────┐
         │   didChangeDependencies()    │
         │   - React to dependencies    │
         └───────────┬──────────────────┘
                     │
         ┌───────────▼──────────────────┐
         │   build() called             │
         │   - Rebuild on state change  │
         │   - Called multiple times    │
         └───────────┬──────────────────┘
                     │
    ┌────────────────┼────────────────┐
    │                │                │
    │         setState() triggered    │
    │                │                │
    └────────────────┼────────────────┘
                     │
         ┌───────────▼──────────────────┐
         │   didUpdateWidget()          │
         │   - Parent widget changed    │
         └───────────┬──────────────────┘
                     │
         ┌───────────▼──────────────────┐
         │   deactivate()               │
         │   - Widget removed           │
         │   - Keep global state        │
         └───────────┬──────────────────┘
                     │
         ┌───────────▼──────────────────┐
         │   dispose()                  │
         │   - Cleanup resources        │
         │   - Cancel subscriptions     │
         │   - Dispose controllers      │
         └───────────┬──────────────────┘
                     │
         ┌───────────▼──────────────────┐
         │   Widget removed             │
         └───────────────────────────────┘
```

**Detailed Implementation:**

```dart
class LifecycleWidget extends StatefulWidget {
  final String title;

  const LifecycleWidget({Key? key, required this.title}) : super(key: key);

  @override
  State<LifecycleWidget> createState() {
    print('LifecycleWidget.createState() - Creating state object');
    return _LifecycleWidgetState();
  }
}

class _LifecycleWidgetState extends State<LifecycleWidget>
    with WidgetsBindingObserver {
  late StreamSubscription _subscription;
  late AnimationController _controller;

  @override
  void initState() {
    super.initState();
    print('initState() - Called ONCE when widget first created');
    
    // Initialize one-time setup
    _subscription = someStream().listen((value) {
      print('Stream value: $value');
    });

    // Setup animation controller
    _controller = AnimationController(
      duration: const Duration(seconds: 2),
      vsync: this,
    );

    // Add lifecycle observer
    WidgetsBinding.instance.addObserver(this);

    // Initialize variables
    print('initState() - Resources initialized');
  }

  @override
  void didChangeDependencies() {
    super.didChangeDependencies();
    print('didChangeDependencies() - Called when widget dependencies change');
    
    // Useful for listening to inherited widgets
    final theme = Theme.of(context);
    print('Theme accessed: ${theme.primaryColor}');
  }

  @override
  void didUpdateWidget(LifecycleWidget oldWidget) {
    super.didUpdateWidget(oldWidget);
    print('didUpdateWidget() - Parent widget changed');
    
    // React to changes in parent widget
    if (oldWidget.title != widget.title) {
      print('Title changed from ${oldWidget.title} to ${widget.title}');
      // Handle title change
    }
  }

  @override
  void deactivate() {
    print('deactivate() - Widget removed from tree');
    // Keep global state, don't dispose yet
    // Will be called before dispose
    super.deactivate();
  }

  @override
  void dispose() {
    print('dispose() - Widget destroyed, cleanup resources');
    
    // Cancel subscriptions
    _subscription.cancel();
    print('Subscription cancelled');

    // Dispose controller
    _controller.dispose();
    print('Animation controller disposed');

    // Remove observer
    WidgetsBinding.instance.removeObserver(this);
    print('Lifecycle observer removed');

    super.dispose();
  }

  @override
  void didChangeAppLifecycleState(AppLifecycleState state) {
    print('App lifecycle changed: $state');
    
    switch (state) {
      case AppLifecycleState.resumed:
        print('App resumed - Resume animations, resume sensors');
        _controller.forward();
        break;
      case AppLifecycleState.inactive:
        print('App inactive - Pause animations');
        break;
      case AppLifecycleState.paused:
        print('App paused - Save state, pause operations');
        _controller.stop();
        break;
      case AppLifecycleState.detached:
        print('App detached - Cleanup');
        break;
    }
  }

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    print('build() - Rendering UI (called many times)');
    
    return Scaffold(
      appBar: AppBar(title: Text(widget.title)),
      body: Center(
        child: Column(
          mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,
          children: [
            Text('Lifecycle Example'),
            ElevatedButton(
              onPressed: () {
                setState(() {
                  print('setState() - Triggering rebuild');
                });
              },
              child: const Text('Trigger Rebuild'),
            ),
          ],
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
}

Stream<int> someStream() async* {
  for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    await Future.delayed(const Duration(seconds: 1));
    yield i;
  }
}
```

**Key Lifecycle Rules:**

| Method | Called | Use Case |
|--------|--------|----------|
| `createState()` | Once | Create state object |
| `initState()` | Once | Initialize resources |
| `didChangeDependencies()` | After initState, on dependency change | Listen to InheritedWidgets |
| `build()` | Multiple times | Render UI |
| `didUpdateWidget()` | When parent rebuilds | React to parent changes |
| `deactivate()` | Before dispose | Prepare for removal |
| `dispose()` | Once | Cleanup resources |

