### 2. State Management - Complete Theory & Patterns

**State Management Theory:**

State management is about managing the data that changes over time and ensuring UI reflects those changes. Different patterns suit different scenarios.

**When to Use Each Pattern:**

```
Simple App (< 5 screens)
    ↓
    Use: setState()
    
─────────────────────────────────────────

Medium App (5-20 screens, moderate complexity)
    ↓
    Use: Provider Pattern
    ├─ Simple to learn
    ├─ Good separation of concerns
    └─ Scales well
    
─────────────────────────────────────────

Complex App (20+ screens, complex logic)
    ↓
    Use: BLoC/Cubit or Riverpod
    ├─ Event-driven architecture
    ├─ Full testability
    └─ Enterprise-level
```

**Provider Pattern - Complete Example:**

```dart
// Theory: Provider notifies widgets when data changes
// Process: Widget listens → Provider updates → Widget rebuilds

// 1. Data Model
class Product {
  final String id;
  final String name;
  final double price;
  final int quantity;

  Product({
    required this.id,
    required this.name,
    required this.price,
    required this.quantity,
  });
}

// 2. Service Layer (Business Logic)
class CartService {
  final List<Product> _cart = [];

  List<Product> get cart => _cart;
  double get total => _cart.fold(0, (sum, item) => sum + (item.price * item.quantity));

  void addItem(Product product) {
    final existing = _cart.firstWhere(
      (item) => item.id == product.id,
      orElse: () => Product(id: '', name: '', price: 0, quantity: 0),
    );

    if (existing.id.isNotEmpty) {
      _cart[_cart.indexOf(existing)] = Product(
        id: existing.id,
        name: existing.name,
        price: existing.price,
        quantity: existing.quantity + 1,
      );
    } else {
      _cart.add(product);
    }
  }

  void removeItem(String productId) {
    _cart.removeWhere((item) => item.id == productId);
  }

  void clear() {
    _cart.clear();
  }
}

// 3. ViewModel (ChangeNotifier - provides state to UI)
class CartViewModel extends ChangeNotifier {
  final CartService _cartService = CartService();

  List<Product> get cart => _cartService.cart;
  double get total => _cartService.total;

  void addItem(Product product) {
    _cartService.addItem(product);
    notifyListeners(); // Notify UI to rebuild
  }

  void removeItem(String productId) {
    _cartService.removeItem(productId);
    notifyListeners();
  }

  void clear() {
    _cartService.clear();
    notifyListeners();
  }
}

// 4. View Layer
void main() {
  runApp(
    ChangeNotifierProvider(
      create: (_) => CartViewModel(),
      child: const MyApp(),
    ),
  );
}

