### 7. Common Patterns & Best Practices

**Repository Pattern:**

```dart
// Theory: Repository abstracts data sources and provides a clean API

abstract class DataRepository {
  Future<List<T>> getAll();
  Future<T> getById(String id);
  Future<void> create(T item);
  Future<void> update(T item);
  Future<void> delete(String id);
}

class UserRepositoryImpl implements UserRepository {
  final RemoteDataSource _remote;
  final LocalDataSource _local;

  UserRepositoryImpl(this._remote, this._local);

  @override
  Future<List<User>> getUsers() async {
    try {
      // Try remote first
      final users = await _remote.getUsers();
      // Cache locally
      await _local.cacheUsers(users);
      return users;
    } catch (e) {
      // Fallback to local
      return await _local.getUsers();
    }
  }
}
```

**Observer Pattern (Using Streams):**

```dart
class NotificationService {
  final _controller = StreamController<String>.broadcast();

  Stream<String> get notifications => _controller.stream;

  void notify(String message) {
    _controller.add(message);
  }

  void dispose() {
    _controller.close();
  }
}

// Usage
final notifier = NotificationService();
notifier.notifications.listen((message) {
  print('Notification: $message');
});
notifier.notify('Hello!');
```

