**Q8: What is the difference between `const` and `final` in Dart?**

A:

| Aspect | const | final |
|--------|-------|-------|
| **Immutability** | Immutable at compile-time | Immutable after initialization |
| **Time** | Compile-time constant | Runtime constant |
| **Memory** | Single instance | New instance per use |
| **Use Case** | Literals, constants | Variables |

**Examples:**
```dart
// const - compile-time constant
const pi = 3.14159;
const List<int> numbers = [1, 2, 3];

// final - runtime constant
final now = DateTime.now();
final name = getUserName(); // Can be function result

// Wrong usage
const now = DateTime.now(); // ❌ Error - DateTime.now() is not const
```

