**Q12: Explain Memory Leaks and how to avoid them in Flutter.**

A: Memory leaks occur when objects are no longer needed but remain in memory.

**Common Causes:**
1. **Not disposing streams:**
```dart
// ❌ Bad - Memory leak
@override
void initState() {
  super.initState();
  myStream.listen((value) { });
}

// ✅ Good
late StreamSubscription _subscription;

@override
void initState() {
  super.initState();
  _subscription = myStream.listen((value) { });
}

@override
void dispose() {
  _subscription.cancel();
  super.dispose();
}
```

2. **Not disposing controllers:**
```dart
// ❌ Bad
final _controller = TextEditingController();

// ✅ Good
@override
void dispose() {
  _controller.dispose();
  super.dispose();
}
```

3. **Global listeners:**
```dart
// ❌ Bad
void initState() {
  WidgetsBinding.instance.addObserver(this);
}

// ✅ Good
@override
void dispose() {
  WidgetsBinding.instance.removeObserver(this);
  super.dispose();
}
```

